  "nl_text": "The rschema_0478 database is designed to manage a bike-sharing system, where users can rent bicycles and record their trips. The database consists of five tables: 'user', 'bicycle', 'trip_record', 'fault_record', and 'billing_rule'. The 'user' table stores information about each user, including their unique identifier, phone number, name, credit, and status. The 'bicycle' table contains details about each bicycle, such as its location, status, and unlock code. The 'trip_record' table tracks each trip made by a user, including the bicycle used, start and end times, cost, payment status, and a reference to the billing rule applied. This table also has a composite primary key consisting of the bicycle ID, user ID, and start time, and foreign keys referencing the 'bicycle' and 'user' tables, which are set to cascade on delete and update. The 'fault_record' table logs any faults reported by users, including the bicycle ID, user ID, reporting time, and fault description, with a composite primary key and foreign keys referencing the 'bicycle' and 'user' tables, also set to cascade on delete and update. The 'billing_rule' table defines the billing rules, including the rule ID, billing method, unit price, and minimum fee, with a primary key on the rule ID.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description for the Shared Bicycle Management System:\nThe shared bicycle company manages multiple users, each with a user ID, phone number, name, credit, and status.\nThe company manages multiple bicycles, each with a bicycle ID, location, status, and unlock code.\nThe company records multiple trips, each trip requiring the recording of user and bicycle usage information, including bicycle number, start time, end time, cost, and payment status.\nThe company manages multiple fault records, each fault involving the user number who encountered the fault, bicycle number, fault description, and reporting time.\nThe company also manages billing rules, each rule including the billing method, unit price, and minimum fee.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0478.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0478\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `credit` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `bicycle` (\n  `bicycle_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `unlock_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`bicycle_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trip_record` (\n  `bicycle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `billing_rule_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`bicycle_id`, `user_id`, `start_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `trip_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`bicycle_id`) REFERENCES `bicycle` (`bicycle_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `trip_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `trip_record_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`billing_rule_id`) REFERENCES `billing_rule` (`rule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `fault_record` (\n  `bicycle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reporting_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `fault_description` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`bicycle_id`, `user_id`, `reporting_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `fault_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`bicycle_id`) REFERENCES `bicycle` (`bicycle_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `fault_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `billing_rule` (\n  `rule_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `billing_method` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `minimum_fee` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rule_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
